{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-38506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the scale factor of the transformation represented by the rotation-scaling matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068112/state.json" "file_sha256" "8937c75733d5dea0bea52ffcdcd4e66478d8fb8e3f4c9e99ac098c77ea213516"} {"question" "q-38506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The scale factor $r$ of the rotation-scaling matrix $[\\begin{aligned}a & -b \\\\ b & a\\end{aligned}]$ can be found using the formula \n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{det(A)}=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068112/state.json" "file_sha256" "8937c75733d5dea0bea52ffcdcd4e66478d8fb8e3f4c9e99ac098c77ea213516"} {"question" "q-38506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068112/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ced3939d8ea075431d5c7a0e9e62a76a6f589d42372d94b3515329b49bf500f7"} {"question" "q-38506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068112/state.json" "file_sha256" "8937c75733d5dea0bea52ffcdcd4e66478d8fb8e3f4c9e99ac098c77ea213516"} {"question" "q-38506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "c